WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.130
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:09.083
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.383 --> 00:00:18.607
Unit sixteen: Writing Task 2: Problems, Solutions and Advantages. Today you will write problem-solution and advantages-disadvantages essays.

4
00:00:18.907 --> 00:00:21.443
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.691
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.412
Problem.

7
00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:31.287
Problem means something difficult that needs a solution.

8
00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:33.848
Traffic is a serious problem.

9
00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:36.870
Your turn. Say: Problem.

10
00:00:39.733 --> 00:00:40.537
Problem.

11
00:00:41.283 --> 00:00:42.203
Solution.

12
00:00:43.217 --> 00:00:45.785
Solution means a way to solve a problem.

13
00:00:46.383 --> 00:00:48.569
One solution is public transport.

14
00:00:49.183 --> 00:00:51.627
Your turn. Say: Solution.

15
00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:55.352
Solution.

16
00:00:56.117 --> 00:00:57.060
Cause.

17
00:00:58.050 --> 00:01:00.491
Cause means the reason something happens.

18
00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:02.955
Pollution has many causes.

19
00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.446
Your turn. Say: Cause.

20
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.255
Cause.

21
00:01:11.017 --> 00:01:11.832
Effect.

22
00:01:12.817 --> 00:01:15.106
Effect means the result of something.

23
00:01:15.717 --> 00:01:17.496
One effect is poor health.

24
00:01:18.083 --> 00:01:20.608
Your turn. Say: Effect.

25
00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:24.259
Effect.

26
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:26.018
Advantage.

27
00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:28.807
Advantage means a good point.

28
00:01:29.417 --> 00:01:31.637
A major advantage is lower cost.

29
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.624
Your turn. Say: Advantage.

30
00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:38.584
Advantage.

31
00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:40.572
Disadvantage.

32
00:01:41.583 --> 00:01:43.571
Disadvantage means a bad point.

33
00:01:44.183 --> 00:01:45.974
A disadvantage is noise.

34
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.154
Your turn. Say: Disadvantage.

35
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.210
Disadvantage.

36
00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:54.812
Outweigh.

37
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:58.002
Outweigh means to be more important than.

38
00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:00.825
The benefits outweigh the costs.

39
00:02:01.417 --> 00:02:03.779
Your turn. Say: Outweigh.

40
00:02:06.633 --> 00:02:07.611
Outweigh.

41
00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:09.281
Implement.

42
00:02:10.283 --> 00:02:12.933
Implement means to put a plan into action.

43
00:02:13.517 --> 00:02:15.772
Governments should implement new laws.

44
00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:18.815
Your turn. Say: Implement.

45
00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:22.633
Implement.

46
00:02:23.433 --> 00:02:27.200
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:31.292
Visal, how do I answer a problem-solution question?

48
00:02:32.383 --> 00:02:44.138
Divide your essay clearly. One body paragraph explains the problems and their causes, and the other body paragraph gives realistic solutions with examples.

49
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:47.575
What about advantages and disadvantages?

50
00:02:48.683 --> 00:03:01.622
Discuss both sides. A common question asks whether the advantages outweigh the disadvantages, so you must give your judgement in the introduction and conclusion.

51
00:03:02.717 --> 00:03:04.832
How can I make solutions convincing?

52
00:03:05.917 --> 00:03:16.464
Explain how each solution works and who should implement it. For example, governments could build cheap public transport, which would reduce traffic and pollution.

53
00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.274
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:20.117 --> 00:03:23.800
Grammar focus: Strategy: answer every part of the question.

55
00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.414
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:31.297
One major problem is traffic; a possible solution is to improve public transport.

57
00:03:32.183 --> 00:03:36.017
Although there are disadvantages, the advantages clearly outweigh them.

58
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:44.820
Check how many parts the question has and answer each one in its own paragraph. Explain solutions step by step and give a clear final judgement.

59
00:03:45.583 --> 00:03:49.536
Be careful! Don't say: I describe only the problems.

60
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.556
Say: I describe problems and solutions.

61
00:03:54.856 --> 00:03:56.263
Answer every part.

62
00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.940
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:00.733 --> 00:04:01.955
Traffic in Cities.

64
00:04:02.255 --> 00:04:05.439
Many cities suffer from heavy traffic and air pollution.

65
00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:09.304
One effect is that people spend hours in their cars.

66
00:04:10.300 --> 00:04:13.867
Governments should implement cheap and reliable public transport.

67
00:04:14.867 --> 00:04:19.142
Although this is expensive, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.

68
00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:23.886
In conclusion, cities need better transport to solve this problem.

69
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.060
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:29.917 --> 00:04:33.727
In a problem-solution essay, one paragraph explains blank.

71
00:04:34.027 --> 00:04:38.761
A, a graph. B, problems and causes. C, a story.

72
00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.542
The answer is B: problems and causes.

73
00:04:46.683 --> 00:04:48.068
'Outweigh' means blank.

74
00:04:48.368 --> 00:04:52.671
A, be lighter than. B, delay. C, be more important than.

75
00:04:56.233 --> 00:04:58.999
The answer is C: be more important than.

76
00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.964
A good solution should be blank.

77
00:05:02.264 --> 00:05:06.869
A, realistic and explained. B, very short. C, unrelated.

78
00:05:10.433 --> 00:05:13.246
The answer is A: realistic and explained.

79
00:05:14.383 --> 00:05:16.325
Who should implement the solution?

80
00:05:16.625 --> 00:05:20.708
A, nobody. B, governments. C, only students.

81
00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:26.313
The answer is B: governments.

82
00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:30.982
According to the reading, what does heavy traffic cause?

83
00:05:31.282 --> 00:05:35.922
A, free time. B, more parks. C, air pollution.

84
00:05:39.467 --> 00:05:42.000
The answer is C: air pollution.

85
00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:46.572
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:47.417 --> 00:05:49.765
How do you write a problem-solution essay?

87
00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.166
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:06:00.466 --> 00:06:17.344
I read the question to see how many parts it has. In one body paragraph I explain the problems and their causes, and in the other I give realistic solutions with explanations and examples. In the conclusion, I summarise the main solution.

89
00:06:17.644 --> 00:06:19.330
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:20.217 --> 00:06:25.621
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: answer every part of the question.

91
00:06:25.921 --> 00:06:31.104
Today's value is practical wisdom. Judge ideas by how well they work in real life.

92
00:06:31.404 --> 00:06:34.056
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:34.356 --> 00:06:37.415
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

